        "bookId": 31,
        "chapterId": 248,
        "headingId": 163,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-04-10T11:41:51"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 364,
    "bookid": 31,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 164,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 55758,
        "bookId": 31,
        "chapterId": 248,
        "headingId": 164,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Histiocytic sarcoma can occur in extranodal or nodal sites, and the GI tract is a common extranodal site of involvement {12121233; 15316312}. Occurrence in the liver, pancreas, gallbladder, or bile ducts is extremely rare.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-04-10T11:41:51"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 365,
    "bookid": 31,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 165,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 55759,
        "bookId": 31,
        "chapterId": 248,
        "headingId": 165,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The most common presentation is intestinal obstruction. Other patients present with abdominal pain or rectal bleeding.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-04-10T11:41:51"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 366,
    "bookid": 31,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 166,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 55760,
        "bookId": 31,
        "chapterId": 248,
        "headingId": 166,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Histiocytic sarcoma is rare. It usually occurs in adults, without sex predilection.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-04-10T11:41:51"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 367,
    "bookid": 31,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 167,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 55761,
        "bookId": 31,
        "chapterId": 248,
        "headingId": 167,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-04-10T11:41:51"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 368,
    "bookid": 31,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 168,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 55762,
        "bookId": 31,
        "chapterId": 248,
        "headingId": 168,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>A subset of cases show clonal IG gene rearrangement {19145200}, particularly when associated with low-grade B-cell lymphoma. This is postulated to represent a transdifferentiation process {24850291; 18272816}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-04-10T11:41:51"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 375,
    "bookid": 31,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 207,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 55763,
        "bookId": 31,
        "chapterId": 248,
        "headingId": 207,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Histiocytic sarcomas are usually solitary masses.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-04-10T11:41:51"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 369,
    "bookid": 31,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 169,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 55764,
        "bookId": 31,
        "chapterId": 248,
        "headingId": 169,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The tumour shows a diffuse proliferation of round to oval large cells with abundant cytoplasm. The nuclei are oval, grooved, or irregularly folded, often with vesicular chromatin and distinct nucleoli. They can exhibit variable degrees of pleomorphism. The cytoplasm is eosinophilic, often with some fine vacuoles. Haemophagocytosis is occasionally observed. The tumour cells can sometimes be spindly. Variable numbers of reactive cells may be admixed. The tumour shows expression of one or more histiocytic markers, including CD163, CD68, and lysozyme, whereas Langerhans cell (CD1a, CD207), follicular dendritic cell (CD21, CD35), and myeloid cell (myeloperoxidase, CD13) markers are negative. There can be heterogeneous expression of S100.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-04-10T11:41:51"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 370,
    "bookid": 31,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 170,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 55765,
        "bookId": 31,
        "chapterId": 248,
        "headingId": 170,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-04-10T11:41:51"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 371,
    "bookid": 31,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 171,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 55766,
        "bookId": 31,
        "chapterId": 248,
        "headingId": 171,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-04-10T11:41:51"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 374,
    "bookid": 31,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 174,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 55767,
        "bookId": 31,
        "chapterId": 248,
        "headingId": 174,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Essential:</em> tumour composed of non-cohesive large cells with abundant eosinophilic cytoplasm; neoplastic cells have reniform, grooved, or irregularly folded nuclei and distinct nucleoli; positive immunostaining for one or more histiocytic markers.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-04-10T11:41:51"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 372,
    "bookid": 31,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 172,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 55768,
        "bookId": 31,
        "chapterId": 248,
        "headingId": 172,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-04-10T11:41:51"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 373,
    "bookid": 31,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 173,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 55769,
        "bookId": 31,
        "chapterId": 248,
        "headingId": 173,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Histiocytic sarcoma is generally an aggressive neoplasm with poor response to therapy. Patients with localized disease and small primary tumours have a more favourable outcome {12121233; 15316312}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2019-04-10T11:41:51"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
]